return {
  ["magicitem.axe-of-the-dwarvish-lords.xdmg2024"]={title="Axe of the Dwarvish Lords",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 231\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nA young dwarf prince set out to forge a weapon that would be regarded as a symbol of unity among his people. Venturing deep under the mountains, deeper than any dwarf had ever delved, the prince came to the blazing heart of a great volcano. With the aid of Moradin, a god of creation, he first crafted four mighty tools: the Starmetal Pick, the Earthheart Forge, the Anvil of Songs, and the Shaping Hammer. With these tools, he forged the Axe of the Dwarvish Lords.\n\nArmed with the Artifact, the prince brought peace to the dwarf clans, ending grudges and answering slights. The clans became allies, and they threw back their enemies and enjoyed an era of prosperity. This young dwarf is remembered as the First King. When he became old, he passed the weapon, which had become his badge of office, to his heir. The rightful inheritors passed the axe on for many generations.\n\nLater, in an era marked by treachery and wickedness, the axe was lost in a bloody civil war fomented by greed for its power and the status it bestowed. Centuries later, the dwarves still search for the axe, and many adventurers have made careers of chasing after rumors and plundering old vaults to find it.\n\nMagic Weapon\n\nThe Axe of the Dwarvish Lords is a magic weapon that grants a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it.\n\nWhen you attack a creature with the axe and roll a 20 on the d20 for the attack roll, the axe deals an extra 20 Slashing damage.\n\nThe axe has XPHB with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When you hit with a ranged attack using this weapon, it deals an extra 1d8 Force damage, or an extra 2d8 Force damage if the target is a creature of the Giant type. Immediately after hitting or missing, the weapon flies back to your hand.\n\nBlessings of Moradin\n\nWhile attuned to the axe, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Darkvision You gain XPHB with a range of 60 feet. If you already have XPHB, its range increases by 60 feet.\n\n• Fortitude of Stone Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20.\n\n• Gifts of the Creator You have proficiency with XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB.\n\n• One with the Forge You have XPHB to Poison damage and XPHB to Fire damage.\n\n• Sunder When you hit an object with the axe, the object takes the maximum amount of damage possible.\n\nConjure Earth Elemental\n\nWhile holding the axe, you can take a XPHB action to summon an XMM. It appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet of yourself, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 24 hours, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB. You can't use this property again until the next dawn.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe axe has the following random properties:\n\n• 2 XDMG properties\n\n• 1 XDMG property\n\n• 2 XDMG properties\n\nTravel the Depths\n\nYou can take a XPHB action to touch the axe to a fixed piece of dwarven stonework and cast XPHB from the axe. If your intended destination is underground, there is no chance of a mishap or arriving somewhere unexpected. You can't use this property again until 3 days have passed.\n\nDestroying the Axe\n\nThe only way to destroy the axe is to melt it down in the Earthheart Forge, where it was created. It must remain in the burning forge for 50 years before it finally succumbs to the fire and is consumed."},
  ["creature.ayik-ur.dsotdq2014"]={title="Ayik Ur",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAttacker\n\nAyik gains a +2 bonus to all attack rolls (included below).\n\nBonus Proficiencies\n\nAyik is proficient with simple and martial weapons, shields, and all armor.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.ayo-jabe-tier-1.crcotn2014"]={title="Ayo Jabe (Tier 1)",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, Orc\n\nResistencias: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nAyo can breathe air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAyo makes two Harpoon or Longbow attacks.\n\nHarpoon\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.ayo-jabe-tier-2.crcotn2014"]={title="Ayo Jabe (Tier 2)",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 97 (15d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, Orc\n\nResistencias: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nAyo can breathe air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAyo makes three Harpoon or Longbow attacks.\n\nHarpoon\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nReposition\n\nAyo issues orders to one ally she can see within 30 feet of herself. If the target can see or hear Ayo, it can spend its reaction to move up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["creature.ayo-jabe-tier-3.crcotn2014"]={title="Ayo Jabe (Tier 3)",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 20 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, Orc\n\nResistencias: acid\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nAyo can breathe air and water.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nAyo wields a ruidium harpoon (see appendix B). If Ayo rolls a 1 on an attack roll made with the harpoon, she must succeed on a 20 Charisma saving throw or gain 1 level of exhaustion.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAyo makes three Harpoon or Longbow attacks.\n\nRuidium Harpoon\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h18 (3d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nReposition\n\nAyo issues orders to one ally she can see within 30 feet of herself. If the target can see or hear Ayo, it can spend its reaction to move up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["creature.ayperobo-swarm.coa2014"]={title="Ayperobo Swarm",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 238\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 130 (20d8 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 60\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 24 | CON 14 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the ayperobo swarm's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe ayperobo swarm has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSwarm\n\nThe ayperobo swarm can occupy another creature's space and vice versa, and the swarm can move through any opening large enough for a Tiny creature. The ayperobo swarm can't regain hit points or gain temporary hit points.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ayperobo swarm makes three Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 0 ft., one target. h27 (8d4 + 7) piercing damage, or 17 (4d4 + 7) piercing damage if the swarm has half of its hit points (65) or fewer.\n\nBurrow {@recharge}\n\nThe ayperobo swarm makes a Bite attack. On a hit, the swarm burrows inside the creature, dealing an additional 35 (10d6) necrotic damage and taking control of the creature. At the start of each of its turns, the target may make a 17 Constitution saving throw, expelling the ayperobo swarm and taking 14 (4d6) piercing damage on a success.\n\nWhile burrowed inside a creature, the ayperobo swarm has Cover against attacks targeting them, and no longer acts on their own initiative. Instead, they take total control over their host, gaining all of its abilities, attacks, and equipment.\n\nThey act during the host's turn, taking actions based on their host. If a host dies while the ayperobo swarm is burrowed, they leave the host at the end of the host's turn, rolling initiative if necessary. Creatures acting as hosts to the ayperobo swarm are fully aware of their actions and surroundings, but are incapable of physically operating their body."},
