to fight alongside you. Choose a bestiary. Add your proficiency bonus to the beast's AC, attack rolls, and damage rolls, as well as to any saving throws and skills it is proficient in. Its hit point maximum equals its normal maximum or four times your ranger level, whichever is higher. Like any creature, the beast can spend Hit Dice during a short rest.\n\nThe beast obeys your commands as best as it can. It takes its turn on your initiative. On your turn, you can verbally command the beast where to move (no action required by you). You can use your action to verbally command it to take the Attack, Dash, Disengage, or Help action. If you don't issue a command, the beast takes the Dodge action. Once you have the Extra Attack feature, you can make one weapon attack yourself when you command the beast to take the Attack action.\n\nIf you are incapacitated or absent, your beast companion acts on its own, focusing on protecting you and itself. It never requires your command to use its reaction, such as when making an opportunity attack.\n\nWhile traveling through your favored terrain with only the beast, you can move stealthily at a normal pace.\n\nIf the beast dies, you can obtain a new companion by spending 8 hours magically bonding with a beast that isn't hostile to you and that meets the requirements.\n\nNivel 3 - Ranger's Companion\n\nNivel 7 - Exceptional Training\n\nPagina: 93\n\nBeginning at 7th level, on any of your turns when your beast companion doesn't attack, you can use a bonus action to command the beast to take the Dash, Disengage, or Help action on its turn. In addition, the beast's attacks now count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.\n\nNivel 7 - Exceptional Training\n\nPagina: 124\n\nWhen you take a XPHB to command your Primal Companion beast to take an action, you can also command it to take the XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB action using its XPHB.\n\nIn addition, whenever it hits with an attack roll and deals damage, it can deal your choice of Force damage or its normal damage type.\n\nNivel 11 - Bestial Fury\n\nPagina: 93\n\nStarting at 11th level, when you command your beast companion to take the Attack action, the beast can make two attacks, or it can take the Multiattack action if it has that action.\n\nNivel 11 - Bestial Fury\n\nPagina: 124\n\nWhen you command your Primal Companion beast to take the Beast's Strike action, the beast can use it twice.\n\nIn addition, the first time each turn it hits a creature under the effect of your XPHB spell, the beast deals extra Force damage equal to the bonus damage of that spell.\n\nNivel 11 - Bestial Fury\n\nNivel 15 - Share Spells\n\nPagina: 93\n\nBeginning at 15th level, when you cast a spell targeting yourself, you can also affect your beast companion with the spell if the beast is within 30 feet of you.\n\nNivel 15 - Share Spells\n\nPagina: 124\n\nWhen you cast a spell targeting yourself, you can also affect your Primal Companion beast with the spell if the beast is within 30 feet of you."},
  ["feature.beast-master.xphb2024.ranger.beast-master.3"]={title="Beast Master",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 123\n\nBond with a Primal Beast\n\nA Beast Master forms a mystical bond with a special animal, drawing on primal magic and a deep connection to the natural world."},
  ["creature.beast-of-malar.fraif2014"]={title="Beast of Malar",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 251\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 168 (16d8 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, burrow: 40, fly: 60, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 16 | CON 23 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious (Sea Form Only)\n\nThe beast breathes air and water.\n\nDivine Immortality\n\nIf the beast dies, its body dissolves into black goo, and it gains a new body after 1d10 days, reviving with all its XPHB in a place of Malar's choosing.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the beast fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe beast has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe beast regains 20 XPHB at the start of its turn. If the beast takes Radiant damage or damage from a XPHB, this trait doesn't function at the start of the beast's next turn. The beast dies only if it starts its turn with 0 XPHB and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe beast makes three attacks, using Bite or Claws in any combination.\n\nBite\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h23 (4d8 + 5) Piercing damage.\n\nClaws (Land or Sky Form Only)\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h18 (3d8 + 5) Slashing damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRecuperative Shape-Shift\n\nThe beast shape-shifts into its land form, sea form, or sky form and regains 9 (2d8) XPHB. Its game statistics are the same in each form, except where noted. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.beast-of-the-land.tce2014"]={title="Beast of the Land",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the beast moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a maul attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 1d6 slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC or be knocked prone.\n\nPrimal Bond\n\nYou can add your proficiency bonus to any ability check or saving throw that the beast makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMaul\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d8 + 2 + PB slashing damage."},
  ["creature.beast-of-the-land.xphb2024"]={title="Beast of the Land",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 123\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you know\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPrimal Bond\n\nAdd your Proficiency Bonus to any ability check or saving throw the beast makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBeast's Strike\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d8 + 2 plus your Wisdom modifier Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage (your choice when you summon the beast). If the beast moved at least 20 feet straight toward the target before the hit, the target takes an extra 1d6 damage of the same type, and the target has the XPHB condition if it is a Large or smaller creature."},
  ["creature.beast-of-the-sea.tce2014"]={title="Beast of the Sea",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, swim: 60\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe beast can breathe both air and water.\n\nPrimal Bond\n\nYou can add your proficiency bonus to any ability check or saving throw that the beast makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBinding Strike\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d6 + 2 + PB piercing damage or 1d6 + 2 + PB bludgeoning damage (your choice), and the target is grappled (escape DC equal to your spellcasting save DC). Until this grapple ends, the beast can't use this attack on another target."},
  ["creature.beast-of-the-sea.xphb2024"]={title="Beast of the Sea",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, swim: 60\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 90 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you know\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe beast can breathe air and water.\n\nPrimal Bond\n\nAdd your Proficiency Bonus to any ability check or saving throw the beast makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBeast's Strike\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d6 + 2 plus your Wisdom modifier Bludgeoning or Piercing damage (your choice when you summon the beast), and the target has the XPHB condition (escape DC equals your spell save DC)."},
  ["creature.beast-of-the-sky.tce2014"]={title="Beast of the Sky",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / S\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe beast doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nPrimal Bond\n\nYou can add your proficiency bonus to any ability check or saving throw that the beast makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShred\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d4 + 3 + PB slashing damage."},
  ["creature.beast-of-the-sky.xphb2024"]={title="Beast of the Sky",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / S\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you know\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe beast doesn't provoke XPHB when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nPrimal Bond\n\nAdd your Proficiency Bonus to any ability check or saving throw the beast makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBeast's Strike\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d4 + 3 plus your Wisdom modifier Slashing damage."},
  ["spell.beast-sense.phb2014"]={title="Beast Sense",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\nYou touch a willing beast. For the duration of the spell, you can use your action to see through the beast's eyes and hear what it hears, and continue to do so until you use your action to return to your normal senses. While perceiving through the beast's senses, you gain the benefits of any special senses possessed by that creature, though you are blinded and deafened to your own surroundings."},
  ["spell.beast-sense.xphb2024"]={title="Beast Sense",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 245\n\nYou touch a willing Beast. For the duration, you can perceive through the Beast's senses as well as your own. When perceiving through the Beast's senses, you benefit from any special senses it has."},
  ["optionalfeature.beast-speech.phb2014"]={title="Beast Speech",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou can cast speak with animals at will, without expending a spell slot."},
  ["feature.beast-spells.phb2014.druid.base.18"]={title="Beast Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nBeginning at 18th level, you can cast many of your druid spells in any shape you assume using Wild Shape. You can perform the somatic and verbal components of a druid spell while in a beast shape, but you aren't able to provide material components."},
  ["feature.beast-spells.xphb2024.druid.base.18"]={title="Beast Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 81\n\nWhile using Wild Shape, you can cast spells in Beast form, except for any spell that has a Material component with a cost specified or that consumes its Material component."},
  ["feature.beasts-of-ill-omen.rhw2014.sorcerer.shadow.6"]={title="Beasts of Ill Omen",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.bebilith.mabjov2014"]={title="Bebilith",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 189 (18d12 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 22 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but only speaks telepathically to its own kind, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDark Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the bebilith's darkvision.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe bebilith can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down, without needing to make an ability check and ignores any movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bebilith uses Poisoned Web (if available) and then makes one Bite attack and two Foreleg attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d12 + 3) piercing damage plus 21 (6d6) poison damage. Any creature that drops to zero hit points because of this attack ignites, suffering 7 (2d6) fire damage at the start of each of its turns until the creature's hit points are above zero.\n\nForeleg\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (4d8 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nPoisoned Web {@recharge 5}\n\nrw 10 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one creature. h51 (10d8 + 6) poison damage, and the target has the restrained condition until free of the web. While restrained, the target takes 9 (2d8) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The target may use an action to make a 17 Strength check and if successful they are freed from the webbing. The webbing can also be attacked and destroyed (AC 12; 10 hit points; immunity to bludgeoning, fire, poison, and psychic damage). If an attack or spell doing fire damage is used on the webbing, the webbing ignites (but is otherwise unharmed). Any creature restrained by the webbing suffers an additional 7 (2d6) fire damage at the start of each of its turn.\n\nStalker's Darkness (3/Day)\n\nThe bebilith casts darkness.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRelentless Hunter\n\nThe bebilith may use a bonus action to mark prey that it has damaged. Only one creature can be marked at a time. The bebilith always knows the exact location of the marked prey on the current plane of existence, can't be surprised by it, and has advantage on all attack rolls against it."},
  ["creature.becklin-uth-viharin.dsotdq2014"]={title="Becklin Uth Viharin",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 55\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.bedroll.phb2014"]={title="Bedroll",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bedroll.xphb2024"]={title="Bedroll",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Bedroll sleeps one Small or Medium creature. While in a Bedroll, you automatically succeed on saving throws against XDMG (see the XDMG)."},
  ["spell.befuddlement.xphb2024"]={title="Befuddlement",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 245\n\nYou blast the mind of a creature that you can see within range. The target makes an Intelligence saving throw.\n\nOn a failed save, the target takes 10d12 Psychic damage and can't cast spells or take the XPHB action. At the end of every 30 days, the target repeats the save, ending the effect on a success. The effect can also be ended by the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB spell.\n\nOn a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."},
  ["optionalfeature.beguiling-arrow.xge2024"]={title="Beguiling Arrow",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 29\n\nYour enchantment magic causes this arrow to temporarily beguile its target. The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 psychic damage, and choose one of your allies within 30 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or it is charmed by the chosen ally until the start of your next turn. This effect ends early if the chosen ally attacks the charmed target, deals damage to it, or forces it to make a saving throw.\n\nThe psychic damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class."},
  ["feature.beguiling-defenses.phb2014.warlock.archfey.10"]={title="Beguiling Defenses",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.beguiling-defenses.xphb2024.warlock.archfey.10"]={title="Beguiling Defenses",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.beguiling-influence.phb2014"]={title="Beguiling Influence",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou gain proficiency in the Deception and Persuasion skills."},
  ["feature.beguiling-magic.xphb2024.bard.glamour.3"]={title="Beguiling Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.beguiling-shot.au2014"]={title="Beguiling Shot",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYour ammunition beguiles your target. The creature you hit takes extra Psychic damage equal to two rolls of your Arcane Shot Die and must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn, treating either you or one of your allies within 30 feet of the target (your choice) as the charmer. The XPHB condition ends early if the charmer attacks the target, deals damage to it, or forces it to make a saving throw."},
  ["feature.beguiling-twist.tce2014.ranger.fey-wanderer.7"]={title="Beguiling Twist",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.beguiling-twist.xphb2024.ranger.fey-wanderer.7"]={title="Beguiling Twist",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.behir.mm2014"]={title="Behir",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 168 (16d12 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, climb: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 90 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe behir makes two attacks: one with its bite and one to constrict.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Large or smaller creature. h17 (2d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 17 (2d10 + 6) slashing damage. The target is grappled (escape 16) if the behir isn't already constricting a creature, and the target is restrained until this grapple ends.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe behir exhales a line of lightning that is 20 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 66 (12d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nSwallow\n\nThe behir makes one bite attack against a Medium or smaller target it is grappling. If the attack hits, the target is also swallowed, and the grapple ends. While swallowed, the target is blinded and restrained, it has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the behir, and it takes 21 (6d6) acid damage at the start of each of the behir's turns. A behir can have only one creature swallowed at a time.\n\nIf the behir takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from the swallowed creature, the behir must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate the creature, which falls prone in a space within 10 feet of the behir. If the behir dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse by using 15 feet of movement, exiting prone."},
  ["creature.behir.xmm2024"]={title="Behir",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 168 (16d12 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, climb: 50\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 90 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe behir makes one Bite attack and uses Constrict.\n\nBite\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h19 (2d12 + 6) Piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) Lightning damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nstr 18, one Large or smaller creature the behir can see within 5 feet. actSaveFail 28 (5d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage. The target has the XPHB condition (escape 16), and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 16, each creature in a 90-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 66 (12d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSwallow\n\ndex 18, one Large or smaller creature XPHB by the behir (the behir can have only one creature swallowed at a time). actSaveFail The behir swallows the target, which is no longer XPHB. While swallowed, a creature has the XPHB and XPHB conditions, has XPHB against attacks and other effects outside the behir, and takes 21 (6d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the behir's turns.\n\nIf the behir takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from the swallowed creature, the behir must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate the creature, which falls in a space within 10 feet of the behir and has the XPHB condition. If the behir dies, a swallowed creature is no longer XPHB and can escape from the corpse by using 15 feet of movement, exiting XPHB."},
  ["creature.beholder.mm2014"]={title="Beholder",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 180 (19d10 + 76)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Undercommon\n\nImunidades a condicoes: prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Cone\n\nThe beholder's central eye creates an area of antimagic, as in the antimagic field spell, in a 150-foot cone. At the start of each of its turns, the beholder decides which way the cone faces and whether the cone is active. The area works against the beholder's own eye rays.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d6) piercing damage.\n\nEye Rays\n\nThe beholder shoots three of the following magical eye rays at random (reroll duplicates), choosing one to three targets it can see within 120 feet of it:\n\n• 1. Charm Ray\n\n• 2. Paralyzing Ray\n\n• 3. Fear Ray\n\n• 4. Slowing Ray\n\n• 5. Enervation Ray\n\n• 6. Telekinetic Ray If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or the beholder moves it up to 30 feet in any direction. It is restrained by the ray's telekinetic grip until the start of the beholder's next turn or until the beholder is incapacitated. If the target is an object weighing 300 pounds or less that isn't being worn or carried, it is moved up to 30 feet in any direction. The beholder can also exert fine control on objects with this ray, such as manipulating a simple tool or opening a door or a container.\n\n• 7. Sleep Ray\n\n• 8. Petrification Ray\n\n• 9. Disintegration Ray If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or take 45 (10d8) force damage. If this damage reduces the creature to 0 hit points, its body becomes a pile of fine gray dust. If the target is a Large or smaller nonmagical object or creation of magical force, it is disintegrated without a saving throw. If the target is a Huge or larger object or creation of magical force, this ray disintegrates a 10-foot cube of it.\n\n• 10. Death Ray\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nEye Ray\n\nThe beholder uses one random eye ray."},
  ["creature.beholder.xmm2024"]={title="Beholder",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 190 (20d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Undercommon\n\nImunidades a condicoes: prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the beholder fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe beholder uses Eye Rays three times.\n\nBite\n\nm 8, reach 5 ft. h13 (3d6 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nEye Rays\n\nThe beholder randomly shoots one of the following magical rays at a target it can see within 120 feet of itself (roll 1d10; reroll if the beholder has already used that ray during this turn):\n\n• 1: Charm Ray wis 16. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition for 1 hour or until it takes damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n• 2: Paralyzing Ray con 16. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n• 3: Fear Ray wis 16. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n• 4: Slowing Ray con 16. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Necrotic damage. Until the end of the target's next turn, the target's XPHB is halved; the target can't take Reactions; and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n• 5: Enervation Ray con 16. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target can't regain XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n• 6: Telekinetic Ray str 16 (the target succeeds automatically if it is Gargantuan). actSaveFail The beholder moves the target up to 30 feet in any direction. The target has the XPHB condition until the start of the beholder's next turn or until the beholder has the XPHB condition. The beholder can also exert fine control on objects with this ray, such as manipulating a tool or opening a door or container.\n\n• 7: Sleep Ray wis 16 (the target succeeds automatically if it is a Construct or an Undead). actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. The condition ends if the target takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it.\n\n• 8: Petrification Ray con 16. 1 The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of its next turn if it is still XPHB, ending the effect on itself on a success. 2 The target has the XPHB condition instead of the XPHB condition.\n\n• 9: Disintegration Ray dex 16. actSaveFail 36 (8d8) Force damage. If the target is a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force, a 10-foot XPHB of it disintegrates into dust. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail If the target is a creature and this damage reduces it to 0 XPHB, it disintegrates into dust.\n\n• 10: Death Ray dex 16. actSaveFail 55 (10d10) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail The target dies if the ray reduces it to 0 XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAntimagic Cone\n\nThe beholder's central eye emits an antimagic wave in a 150-foot XPHB. Until the start of the beholder's next turn, that area acts as an XPHB spell, and that area works against the beholder's own Eye Rays.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nChomp\n\nThe beholder makes two Bite attacks.\n\nGlare\n\nThe beholder uses Eye Rays."},
  ["creature.beholder-zombie.mm2014"]={title="Beholder Zombie",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 316\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 8 | CON 16 | INT 3 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Deep Speech and Undercommon but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 + the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d6) piercing damage.\n\nEye Ray\n\nThe zombie uses a random magical eye ray, choosing a target that it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n• 1. Paralyzing Ray\n\n• 2. Fear Ray\n\n• 3. Enervation Ray\n\n• 4. Disintegration Ray If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Dexterity saving throw or take 45 (10d8) force damage. If this damage reduces the creature to 0 hit points, its body becomes a pile of fine gray dust. If the target is a Large or smaller nonmagical object or creation of magical force, it is disintegrated without a saving throw. If the target is a Huge or larger nonmagical object or creation of magical force, this ray disintegrates a 10-foot cube of it."},
  ["creature.beholder-zombie.xmm2024"]={title="Beholder Zombie",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 347\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 8 | CON 16 | INT 3 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Deep Speech and Undercommon but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the zombie to 0 XPHB, it makes a Constitution saving throw (5 plus the damage taken) unless the damage is Radiant or from a XPHB. On a successful save, the zombie drops to 1 XPHB instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe zombie uses Eye Rays twice.\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h16 (4d6 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nEye Rays\n\nThe zombie randomly shoots one of the following magical rays at a target it can see within 120 feet of itself (roll 1d4; reroll if the zombie has already used that ray during this turn):\n\n• 1: Paralyzing Ray con 14. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n• 2: Fear Ray wis 14. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n• 3: Enervation Ray con 14. actSaveFail 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target can't regain XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n• 4: Disintegration Ray dex 14. actSaveFail 27 (5d10) Force damage. If the target is a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force, a 10-foot XPHB of it disintegrates into dust. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail If the target is a creature and this damage reduces it to 0 XPHB, it disintegrates into dust."},
  ["background.bejeweled-conclave-spy.au2014"]={title="Bejeweled Conclave Spy",subtitle="Background - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["item.bejeweled-conclave-trinket.au2014"]={title="Bejeweled Conclave Trinket",subtitle="Item - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\nRaridade: none\n\n1d6 | Trinket\n\n1 | An empty perfume bottle that smells faintly of longing\n\n2 | Three love letters in the same handwriting, signed with different names\n\n3 | A silk scarf with several hidden pockets\n\n4 | The signature page from a contract\n\n5 | A drinking glass carved with a comet\n\n6 | A gaudy engagement ring with a fake gem"},
  ["item.bejeweled-gold-bracelet.xdmg2024"]={title="Bejeweled gold bracelet",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bejeweled-ivory-drinking-horn-with-gold-filigree.dmg2014"]={title="Bejeweled ivory drinking horn with gold filigree",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bejeweled-ivory-drinking-horn-with-gold-filigree.xdmg2024"]={title="Bejeweled ivory drinking horn with gold filigree",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bejeweled-ivory-drinking-horn-with-gold-inlay-brazen-coalition.psx2014"]={title="Bejeweled ivory drinking horn with gold inlay (Brazen Coalition)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.bel.bgdia2014"]={title="Bel",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 364 (27d10 + 216)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 26 | INT 25 | WIS 19 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nAny creature hostile to Bel that starts its turn within 20 feet of him must make a 23 Wisdom saving throw, unless Bel is incapacitated. Unless the save succeeds, the creature is frightened until the start of its next turn. If a creature's saving throw is successful, the creature is immune to Bel's Fear Aura for the next 24 hours.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Bel fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nBel has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nBel's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBel makes three attacks: two with his greatsword and one with his tail.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h23 (4d6 + 9) slashing damage plus 21 (6d6) fire damage. If the target is a flammable object that is not being held or worn, it catches fire.\n\nTail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h25 (3d10 + 9) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFireball\n\nBel casts fireball.\n\nTactical Edge (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nRoll a d6 for Bel. The number rolled on the die is subtracted from the next attack roll made against Bel or an ally of his choice within the next minute.\n\nSummon Ice Devil (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nBel magically summons an ice devil with an ice spear (as described in the ice devil's entry in the Monster Manual). The ice devil appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of Bel, acts as Bel's ally, and can summon other devils if it has such power. The ice devil remains until Bel dies or until he dismisses it as an action."},
  ["creature.bel.coa2014"]={title="Bel",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 364 (27d10 + 216)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 26 | INT 25 | WIS 19 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nAny creature hostile to Bel that starts its turn within 20 feet of him must make a 23 Wisdom saving throw unless Bel is incapacitated. If the save fails, the creature has the frightened condition until the start of its next turn. If a creature's saving throw is successful, the creature is immune to Bel's Fear Aura for the next 24 hours.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Bel fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nBel has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBel attacks twice with his Greatsword and once with his Tail.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h23 (4d6 + 9) slashing damage plus 21 (6d6) fire damage. If the target is a flammable object that isn't being held or worn, it catches fire.\n\nTail\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h25 (3d10 + 9) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFireball\n\nBel casts Fireball.\n\nTactical Edge (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nRoll a d6 for Bel. The number rolled on the die is subtracted from the next attack roll made against Bel or an ally of his choice within the next minute.\n\nSummon Ice Devil (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nBel magically summons an ice devil with an ice spear (as described in the ice devil's entry in the Monster Manual). The ice devil appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of Bel, acts as Bel's ally, and can summon other devils if it has such power. The ice devil remains until Bel dies or until he dismisses it with an action."},
  ["creature.belak-the-outcast.tftyp2014"]={title="Belak the Outcast",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 11/16\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Druidic plus any two languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit (4 to hit with shillelagh), reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage with shillelagh or if wielded with two hands."},
  ["creature.belashyrra.erlw2014"]={title="Belashyrra",subtitle="Criatura - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 286\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 304 (32d8 + 160)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 21 | CON 20 | INT 25 | WIS 22 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAlien Mind\n\nIf a creature tries to read Belashyrra's thoughts or deals psychic damage to it, that creature must succeed on a 22 Intelligence saving throw or be stunned for 1 minute. The stunned creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nEye Thief\n\nBelashyrra can see through the eyes of all creatures within 120 feet of it. It can use its Eye Ray through any creature within 120 feet of it, as though it were in that creature's space.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Belashyrra fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nBelashyrra has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nBelashyrra regains 20 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of its next turn. Belashyrra dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nTeleport\n\nAs a bonus action, Belashyrra can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBelashyrra makes two attacks with its claws and uses its Eye Ray once.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (3d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nEye Ray\n\nBelashyrra shoots one of the following magical eye rays of its choice, targeting one creature it can see within 120 feet of it:\n\n• 1. Psyche-Reconstruction Ray\n\n• 2. Domination Ray\n\n• 3. Mind-Weakening Ray\n\n• 4. Blinding Ray\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nBelashyrra makes one claw attack.\n\nImplant Fear (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nBelashyrra targets a creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or take 22 (4d10) psychic damage and immediately use its reaction, if available, to move as far as its speed allows away from Belashyrra.\n\nRend Reality (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nBelashyrra rips at the bonds of reality in its immediate area. Each creature within 10 feet of Belashyrra must succeed on a 22 Constitution saving throw or take 19 (3d12) force damage and gain one level of exhaustion."},
  ["magicitem.belashyrra-s-beholder-crown.erlw2014"]={title="Belashyrra's Beholder Crown",subtitle="Item Magico - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis symbiotic crown is carved from dark purple and mauve stone, with ten points like stalks set with gemstones resembling the eyestalks of a beholder. To attune to this item, you must wear it on your head for the entire attunement period, during which the crown's hidden tendrils burrow into your scalp to bond with your skull.\n\nWhile wearing the crown, you can see normally in darkness, both magical and nonmagical, to a distance of 120 feet.\n\nSpells\n\nThe crown has 10 charges. While wearing it, you can use an action to expend some of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it (spell save 16): charm person (1 charge), disintegrate (6 charges), fear (3 charges), finger of death (7 charges), flesh to stone (6 charges), hold person (2 charges), ray of enfeeblement (2 charges), sleep (1 charge), slow (3 charges), telekinesis (5 charges).\n\nThe crown regains 1d6 + 3 expended charges daily at dawn.\n\nSymbiotic Nature\n\nThe crown can't be removed from you while you're attuned to it, and you can't voluntarily end your attunement to it. If you're targeted by a spell that ends a curse, your attunement to the crown ends, and it detaches from you.\n\nThe daelkyr ERLW made these crowns. While on the same plane of existence as the crown, Belashyrra can see through its eyestalks."},
  ["creature.beldora.skt2014"]={title="Beldora",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 249\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 18 (4d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 16 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRoleplaying Information\n\nBeldora is a member of the harpers who survives using her wits and wiles. She looks like a homeless waif, but she's a survivor who shies away from material wealth.\n\nIdeal: \"We should all strive to help one another\"\n\nBond: \"I'll risk my life to protect the powerless.\"\n\nFlaw: \"I like lying to people. Makes life more interesting, no?\"\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage. Beldora carries ten crossbow bolts.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDuck and Cover\n\nBeldora adds 2 to her AC against one ranged attack that would hit her. To do so, Beldora must see the attacker and can't be grappled or restrained."},
  ["creature.beledros-witherbloom.scc2014"]={title="Beledros Witherbloom",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 186\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 444 (24d20 + 192)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 27 | INT 18 | WIS 28 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Druidic, Sylvan\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Beledros fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nBeledros doesn't require air, food, or drink.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBeledros makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h14 (1d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (1d6 + 9) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is knocked prone.\n\nDecaying Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nBeledros exhales decaying energy in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 23 Constitution saving throw, taking 39 (6d12) necrotic damage and 39 (6d12) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that takes damage from the breath can't regain hit points until the start of Beledros's next turn.\n\nMiasmal Flow\n\nBeledros becomes a swirling cloud of green mist and can move up to half her flying speed without provoking opportunity attacks, then resumes her true form. During this movement, she can move through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. If she moves through a creature, it must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned until the end of its next turn. If Beledros ends this move inside an object, she takes 5 (1d10) force damage and is shunted to the nearest unoccupied space.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nBeledros makes one Claw attack.\n\nMiasmal Flow (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nBeledros uses Miasmal Flow.\n\nTeeming with Life (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nBeledros magically summons 1d4 SCC in unoccupied spaces she can see within 60 feet of herself. The pests obey her commands and take their turns immediately after hers. Any creature, other than a pest, takes 9 (2d8) poison damage if it starts its turn within 5 feet of one or more of these pests. When one of these pests drops to 0 hit points, Beledros regains 9 hit points. These pests disappear after 10 minutes, when Beledros dies, or when she uses this action again."},
  ["deity.belenus.phb2014"]={title="Belenus",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["creature.belephaion.dsotdq2014"]={title="Belephaion",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.belial.coa2014"]={title="Belial",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 420 (40d8 + 240)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 17 | CON 22 | INT 22 | WIS 22 | CHA 29\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeep Wounds\n\nAll damage dealt by Belial can only be restored through magical means.\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Belial's darkvision.\n\nFear Aura\n\nWhen a creature starts their turn within 120 feet of Belial, they must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or have the frightened condition until they leave the aura. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to this effect for 1 hour.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nBelial regains 20 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Belial dies only if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Belial fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nBelial has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBelial makes three attacks using his Ranseur of Torture.\n\nRanseur of Torture\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) necrotic damage, and the target must make a 23 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target's movement speed is reduced by 5 feet until the end of their next turn. This penalty can stack.\n\nWalls of Phlegethos\n\nBelial creates a wall of fire on a solid surface within 120 feet of him. The wall is 20 feet high and 1 foot thick, and Belial can make the wall up to 60 feet long or create a ringed wall up to 20 feet in diameter. The wall is opaque and lasts until Belial dismisses it. When the wall appears, each creature within its area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that ends its turn inside the wall, or within 5 feet of it, must repeat the save.\n\nSymbol of Insanity {@recharge 4}\n\nBelial draws a magic symbol at a point he can see within 120 feet of him. All creatures within a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on the symbol must make a 25 Intelligence saving throw. Targets take 45 (10d8) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Creatures that fail the save immediately use their reaction to make a melee attack against a random creature within their reach, then move their full movement in a random direction.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nPleasure in Pain\n\nAs a reaction to taking damage, Belial immediately regenerates half the damage he took.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nRanseur\n\nBelial makes a Ranseur of Torture attack.\n\nEruption (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nBelial causes molten stone to erupt from a point he can see within 90 feet of him. All creatures within a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw. Targets take 28 (8d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nBelial summons an allied horned devil in an unoccupied space that he can see."},
  ["item.bell.phb2014"]={title="Bell",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bell.xphb2024"]={title="Bell",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhen rung as a XPHB action, a Bell produces a sound that can be heard up to 60 feet away."},
  ["magicitem.bell-branch.tce2014"]={title="Bell Branch",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis silver implement is shaped like a tree branch and is strung with small golden bells. The branch is a spellcasting focus for your spells while you hold it.\n\nThe branch has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. You can use the charges in the following ways while holding it:\n\n• As a bonus action, you can expend 1 charge to detect the presence of aberrations, celestials, constructs, elementals, fey, fiends, or undead within 60 feet of you. If such creatures are present and don't have Cover from you, the bells ring softly, their tone indicating the creature types present.\n\n• As an action, you can expend 1 charge to cast protection from evil and good."},
  ["magicitem.bellows-of-strangulation.au2014"]={title="Bellows of Strangulation",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis bellows has 6 charges. While you are holding it, you can take a XPHB action and use one of three command words to cause one of the following effects:\n\n• First Command Word\n\n• Second Command Word\n\n• Third Command Word\n\nRegaining Charges\n\nThe bellows regains 1d6 + 1 charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the bellows explodes in a harmless burst of wind and is lost forever."},
  ["magicitem.belt-of-cloud-giant-strength.dmg2014"]={title="Belt of Cloud Giant Strength",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhile wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 27. The item has no effect on you if your Strength without the belt is equal to or greater than the belt's score."},
  ["magicitem.belt-of-cloud-giant-strength.xdmg2024"]={title="Belt of Cloud Giant Strength",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 236\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhile wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 27. The item has no effect on you if your Strength without the belt is equal to or greater than the belt's score."},
  ["magicitem.belt-of-dwarvenkind.dmg2014"]={title="Belt of Dwarvenkind",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this belt, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Your Constitution score increases by 2, to a maximum of 20.\n\n• You have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to interact with dwarves.\n\nIn addition, while attuned to the belt, you have a 50 chance each day at dawn of growing a full beard if you're capable of growing one, or a visibly thicker beard if you already have one.\n\nIf you aren't a dwarf, you gain the following additional benefits while wearing the belt:\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against poison, and you have resistance against poison damage.\n\n• You have darkvision out to a range of 60 feet.\n\n• You can speak, read, and write Dwarvish."},
  ["magicitem.belt-of-dwarvenkind.xdmg2024"]={title="Belt of Dwarvenkind",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 235\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this belt, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Dwarvish You know Dwarvish.\n\n• Friend of Dwarvenkind You have XPHB on Charisma (XPHB) checks made to interact with dwarves and duergar.\n\n• Toughness Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20.\n\n• In addition, while attuned to the belt, you have a 50 chance each day at dawn of growing a full beard if you can grow one, or a thicker beard if you already have one.\n\n• If you aren't a dwarf or duergar, you gain the following additional benefits while wearing the belt:\n\n• Darkvision You have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\n• Resilience You have XPHB to Poison damage. You also have XPHB on saving throws you make to avoid or end the XPHB condition."},
  ["magicitem.belt-of-fire-giant-strength.dmg2014"]={title="Belt of Fire Giant Strength",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 25. The item has no effect on you if your Strength without the belt is equal to or greater than the belt's score."},
  ["magicitem.belt-of-fire-giant-strength.xdmg2024"]={title="Belt of Fire Giant Strength",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 236\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 25. The item has no effect on you if your Strength without the belt is equal to or greater than the belt's score."},
